THE DEEP ROAD — a dwarf campaign

Chronicle of Warden Brakka Stonewrit, Third Seal of Khaz Mordun.

For two hundred years the Deep Road lay shut. Our grandmothers collapsed its far galleries themselves, and carved into the sealing stone a single word: ENOUGH.

Last night the word cracked.

Goblins came through the Undergate with the dawn bell — not a raid, a flood. The outer farms are burning. Old Warden Dolgrim held the stair with a shield and a bad knee, and bought us the hour we are spending now.

I have three names on my muster roll. Thorin Emberhand, warrior, who argues with anvils and wins. Vala Leadrain, thunderer, who can put a bolt through a keyhole at forty paces. And Muni the Door — guard of the Third Seal, slow as guilt and about as movable.

Three dwarves. One road. It will have to be enough.

The goblins hold the Gates. We take them back first.
